#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0546 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), PCHGCA1N(Num), PCHGCAT1(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1 | DECREASED`. Both halves of the pair are declared, so the second conjunct `not var_exists('PCHGCAT1')` is FALSE and the rule is silent. The two wildcard patterns are disjoint, so this still yields exactly one expansion (y=1), not two."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col PCHGCA1N type=Num
col PCHGCAT1 type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1 | DECREASED
